## Unresolved

Nothing blocking. The only judgment call worth flagging: the P2-1 tests simulate the post-throw state rather than throwing literally from a timer callback — both because a real throw is process-fatal on Node and zone-swallowed-or-worse under cljd.test, and because the liveness property the fix guarantees ("a body that fails before its own arm never leaves the owner unarmed") is exactly what the simulation exercises. The reviewer's own alternative-fix framing ("arm a fallback at the start of the tick and let the final `arm!` replace it") is the shape shipped.
